# Instruction authoring

## When and boundaries

Use for durable triggered engineering rules. Not a substitute for a feature plan,
architecture reference, release history, native skill or client security policy.

## Procedure

1. Search {{instruction_catalog_and_owner_map}} for an existing responsibility.
   Update it when audience, invariants and update causes match. Create only for a
   distinct recurring responsibility/trigger, not a task-specific report or filename.
2. Read the full affected instruction and relevant current contracts. Establish
   actual code owners/paths/symbols and consumers; source inspection confirms what
   is implemented, not whether a defect should be legitimized.
3. Record finite paths and dirty intersections. Use {{profiled_instruction_form_route}}:
   trigger, scope/non-goals, owner/contract, practical steps, constraints with reasons,
   sufficient checks/limits, related sources and update conditions. Keep one canonical
   body; no duplicated philosophy or independently editable tables of the same rule.
4. `read_when` names concrete tasks/files/contracts and terms. Commands specify real
   environment, input, side effects and permission boundaries. Useful negative cases
   belong with checks. Fictional APIs or assumed test commands do not become rules.
5. Add catalog trigger and nearest daily route. Preserve required native routing
   fields/adapters until their real consumer is migrated. A manual path is sufficient
   for explicit reading; automatic loading needs client-specific proof. A missing
   out-of-scope consumer is an exact integration handoff, not silent scope expansion.
6. Run {{verified_documentation_check_or_unconfigured}} and inspect exact diff, source
   consistency and actual routes. Report raw exits/unrun checks. Follow the project's
   acceptance/save policy; freeze for independent review when required, without a
   second review layer. A new instruction does not self-accept or change that policy.

## Sync versus policy

Updating a command after an accepted tool move is technical synchronization.
Allowing expenses, changing data protection, weakening a test, removing independent
review, expanding access or publishing is policy, even if presented as a small edit.
Require the policy owner's explicit decision; continue unrelated permitted work.
Never change a requirement just to match a bug or obtain green checks.

## Maintenance

Update when the owner/contract, command, consumer, invariant or permission changes.
Preserve the project's native AGENTS/SKILL grammar; ordinary note frontmatter is not
mechanically imposed on special formats or global profiles. Scope limits remain.
